# <type>(<scope>): <subject line (imperative, present tense, max 72 chars)>
# ─── Example: feat(lab): add automated AD Domain Controller install ───

# Why is this change necessary?
# - What problem does this commit solve?
# - What was the motivation for this change?

# Summary of changes:
# - Bullet points of key technical changes
# - Side effects, migrations, or architectural impacts

# Breaking changes & References:
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
# Closes #<issue> / Fixes #<issue>

# ─── Allowed Types ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# feat:     A new feature or functionality
# fix:      A bug fix
# security: Security hardening, CVE patch, or permission fix
# docs:     Documentation changes only
# refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
# perf:     A code change that improves performance
# test:     Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
# build:    Changes affecting the build system or external dependencies
# ci:       Changes to CI/CD workflows and automation scripts
# chore:    Tooling, maintenance, repo configuration, templates
# revert:   Revert a previous commit
#
# ─── Allowed Scopes (AtlasTech) ───────────────────────────────────────
# api:       services/api (FastAPI, SQLAlchemy models, routes, engine)
# web:       apps/web (Next.js 15, dashboard, fleet table, triage desk)
# collector: agents/collector (PowerShell telemetry collector)
# infra:     infra/ (Docker, Vagrant, AD, DNS, domain scripts)
# lab:       infra/lab (Lab environment VMs, provisioning)
# chaos:     infra/chaos (Fault injection playbooks)
# schemas:   packages/schemas (Shared TypeScript schemas & contracts)
# docs:      Documentation, ADRs, runbooks, architecture
# git:       Git configuration, hooks, commit templates
# deps:      Dependency updates and management
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
